Notebook[{Cell["CGCoefficients", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["CGCoefficients[g, {p, q}, targets] gives CGData with every copy of \
every selected target irrep in the tensor product of the irreps p and q of \
the group or context g: embeddings K with R.K == K.D and duals W with W.R == \
D.W on every recorded generator, normalized and validated. targets is All \
(default), an irrep ID or a list.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["CGCoefficients[g, {p, q}, targets] gives Clebsch-Gordan \
coefficients of the irreps p and q of a group or RepresentationContext: every \
copy of every selected target (All, an irrep ID or a list), with K satisfying \
R.K == K.D and W satisfying W.R == D.W on every recorded generator.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["Normalization Automatic gives orthonormal copies with W = \
K^dagger for unitary matrices and dual-paired copies (W_a.K_b = delta_ab I) \
for general bases. Equal factors (the same stored variant) are split into \
symmetric and antisymmetric sectors.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Method Automatic uses the documented routes (GeneratorEquations, \
ProjectionLazy, SubgroupChain, AveragedBSGS, SerreBSGS, Serre, \
CanonicalHybrid, AveragedIntertwiners, AveragedOrbit, SubgroupEmbedding, \
CommutantSpectral, AdaptedStates, ProjectionEager), the Wolfram routes before \
the native GAP routes; stored coefficients are used first (with an explicit \
Method, a note names the method that made them). Exact results are proved \
exactly; Arithmetic -> \"Numerical\" gives verified numerical coefficients.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["With CoreBudget of four or more, Method Automatic runs the \
Wolfram routes of a batch at the same time in Wolfram subkernels and takes \
the first result that validates in the calling kernel; the others are \
stopped. The subkernels are kept for the session (CloseCGPool closes them) \
and are not used while other parallel kernels run; stopping a race also \
cancels any other ParallelSubmit job queued on them. The winning route can \
differ between calls, so a repeated target may come with another valid phase \
or multiplicity basis; an explicit Method gives a reproducible choice. Under \
Method Automatic, CommutantSpectral and AdaptedStates are used only for \
stored unitary matrices, and SubgroupEmbedding only with subgroup information \
(MethodData, or a recorded proper subgroup).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Group calls store new coefficients in the group's Wolfram CG store \
(one atomic commit per call, reported under \"Publication\" -> \
<|\"Published\" -> n|>; no GAP work) and may compute missing representations \
with GAP. When another target fails, the validated targets are still stored \
and the failure's Coverage lists AcceptedTargets, ComputedTargets, \
FailedTargets and PendingTargets. Context calls never store coefficients; the \
native GAP routes (SubgroupChain, AveragedBSGS, Serre, SerreBSGS) still run \
their worker query on the live group, which advances its state generation \
without changing its data.", "Notes"], Cell["FieldMethod chooses the exact \
arithmetic domain and Verification how coefficients are checked (Automatic, \
\"Exact\", \"Numerical\" or None); both can be session defaults \
(ConfigureVVMFTool). The CGData records each target's domain and verification \
status under \"Provenance\" and the weakest status under \
\"VerificationStatus\".", "Notes"], Cell["Method may also be an ordered list \
of routes, tried one at a time in that order in the calling kernel (no race); \
members that do not apply are skipped and reported in the attempts. With an \
explicit Method, a target already stored is returned from the store with a \
note naming the method that made it; Recompute -> True computes it with the \
requested method (returned, stored only where nothing is stored).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Method"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Normalization"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic (default) resolves from the participating matrices; \
\"Unitary\" or \"Dual\" fix the convention.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["ExchangeSymmetry"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic (default), \"Separate\" or None.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Arithmetic"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["\"Exact\"", "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\" proves identities \
exactly and refuses numerical input; \"Numerical\" works at WorkingPrecision \
(default 50) and checks residuals against Tolerance (default \
10^(-Floor[p/2])). Tolerance is accepted only with numerical arithmetic.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["WorkingPrecision"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["50", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Tolerance"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Prefilter"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True (default) or False.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["NumberField"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic (default), True or False.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["MethodData"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["<|\"SubgroupGenerators\" -> {GroupWord..}, \
\"Representation\" -> Rep|> for CharacterSubgroup, Induction, InducedUnitary, \
Extension and NormalExtension (the Representation is optional and not used by \
CharacterSubgroup); <|\"AtlasName\" -> name, \"RepresentationNumber\" -> n|> \
for AtlasRep.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["ComputeMissingRepresentations"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True (default) or False.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["StoreGAPState"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True retains verified state across \
calls; False keeps only call-local temporary checkpoints. Cached mathematical \
values remain available.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["AttemptTimeLimit"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["600", "TableText"], Cell["Positive seconds or Infinity, per \
attempt including verification and saving. Automatic method attempts each \
receive this limit.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["CoreBudget"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer at most $ProcessorCount, or \
Automatic to use the available count. Sequential algorithms run as separate \
worker processes.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["MemoryBudget"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer bytes, or Automatic using half \
system memory less current kernel usage. Admission estimates and sampled \
total worker RSS enforce the allocation.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["ProgressFunction"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic shows a \
notebook monitor when a front end is available; None is silent; a Function or \
user symbol receives progress associations. Callbacks should return promptly; \
failures/cancellation clean owned workers.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["FieldMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Cyclotomic\", \
\"PrimitiveElement\", \"Radical\", \"RootReduce\" or a duplicate-free list of \
these.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Verification"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Exact\", \"Numerical\" or None (the \
Validate functions: Automatic, \"Exact\" or \"Numerical\"; the modular-form \
functions have no \"Exact\" route).", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Recompute"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["False", "TableText"], Cell["True or False.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["UnitarizationMethod"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["\"GroupAverage\" \
averages M^\[Dagger].M over the image of the group; \"GeneratorEquations\" \
solves M^\[Dagger].H.M == H on the generators and chooses a positive \
solution; \"BSGSAverage\" is a native GAP route (automatic representation \
computation and TransformGroupRepresentations in GAP) and is refused where \
the work runs in Wolfram.", "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> 
      {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], Scaled[0.18], 
         Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
  Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["CGIntertwiners", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CGIntertwiners.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["CGMatrix", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CGMatrix.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ValidateCG", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ValidateCG.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["CacheCG", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CacheCG.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["TensorProductVectors", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"TensorProductVectors.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["CloseCGPool", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CloseCGPool.nb", None}]}], "SeeAlso"], 
  Cell["Examples Initialization", "ExamplesInitializationSection"], 
  Cell["Open this notebook in its repository location. GAP must be installed; \
LINS is required for its bounded search page. Evaluate the setup before the \
examples.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Nest", "[", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", 
                  ",", RowBox[{"NotebookFileName", "[", "]"}], ",", "5"}], 
                "]"}], ",", "\"Kernel\"", ",", "\"init.m\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ";"}]], "ExampleInitialization"], 
  Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", 
                "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"GroupPresentation", "[", RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s\"", ",", "\"t\""}], "}"}], 
                      ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s^2\"", ",", "\"t^2\"", 
                          ",", "\"(s.t)^3\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            ",", "d"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[
         {RowBox[{"d", "=", RowBox[{"First", "[", RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"IrrepOrder\"", "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"RepDim", "[", RowBox[
                         {"GroupRepresentation", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                          "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "===", "2"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"Length", "[", RowBox[{"CGIntertwiners", 
              "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"CGCoefficients", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"d", ",", "d"}], "}"}], ",", 
                    "All"}], "]"}], ",", "d"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], 
   "Input", CellTags -> "VerifiedExample"], Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output"], 
  Cell["Possible Issues", "ExampleSection"], Cell["Invalid input returns a \
structured Failure. Check FailureQ before using the result.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"FailureQ", "[", RowBox[{"CGCoefficients", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"no group\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", 
              "\"b\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellTags -> "VerifiedErrorExample"], Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], 
  Cell["Related Guides", "MoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Constructing finite groups", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"../../Tutorials/ConstructingFiniteGroups.nb", None}]}], 
